# 3D Interactive Parallax Application

Build an immersive 3D web application that responds to **device motion** (mobile tilt), **face detection** (head-tracking parallax), and **mouse/trackpad movement** (desktop fallback) to create a depth-rich, living 3D scene.

## Technology Choices

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Three.js** (r162 via CDN) | 3D rendering, lighting, post-processing |
| **TensorFlow.js + Face Landmarks Detection** | Real-time face/head position tracking via webcam |
| **Device Orientation API** | Mobile gyroscope-based parallax |
| **Mouse/Trackpad Events** | Desktop fallback for parallax |

## Proposed Changes

### Application Structure

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/index.html)
- Completely rewrite to serve as the main entry point
- Include CDN links for Three.js, TensorFlow.js, and Face Landmarks Detection
- Add a fullscreen canvas with UI overlay showing current tracking mode

#### [NEW] [style.css](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/style.css)
- Dark theme with glassmorphism UI overlay
- Mode indicator badges (Mouse / Gyroscope / Face Tracking)
- Loading screen with animated spinner
- Smooth transitions and micro-animations

#### [NEW] [app.js](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/app.js)
Core application module containing:
1. **3D Scene**: Multi-layered floating geometric objects (icosahedrons, torus knots, octahedrons) at different depths
2. **Parallax System**: Objects at different Z-depths move at different rates based on input, creating a true 3D feel
3. **Particle Field**: Hundreds of tiny glowing particles for atmospheric depth
4. **Input Managers**:
   - `MouseTracker` — maps cursor position to camera offset
   - `DeviceMotionTracker` — uses `DeviceOrientationEvent` for mobile tilt
   - `FaceTracker` — uses TensorFlow.js Face Landmarks to track head position via webcam
5. **Lighting**: Ambient + multiple colored point lights that subtly shift
6. **Post-processing**: Bloom/glow effect for a premium feel

## How It Works

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Mouse Movement] --> D[Parallax Engine]
    B[Device Gyroscope] --> D
    C[Face Detection] --> D
    D --> E[Camera Offset]
    E --> F[3D Scene Layers Move]
    F --> G[Depth Illusion]
```

- **Desktop**: Mouse position creates parallax camera shifts
- **Mobile**: Tilting the device shifts the viewpoint via gyroscope
- **Face Detection**: Webcam tracks your face/head position; moving your head left/right/up/down shifts the 3D perspective as if you're looking through a window

## Verification Plan

### Browser Testing
1. Open [index.html](file:///Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app/index.html) in a local dev server: `npx -y serve /Users/apple/Kvs/3d_app`
2. **Mouse parallax**: Move mouse around — 3D objects should shift with depth parallax
3. **Face tracking**: Click the face-tracking toggle — webcam should activate and head movement should control the parallax
4. **Visual quality**: Scene should have bloom/glow, floating particles, and smooth animations
5. **Mobile**: Open on phone on same network — tilting device should shift the 3D perspective
